# QA / release / reporting

## Accounts

Do **not** mutate **Sora** or **Twinkle** in automated QA unless the owner authorizes that exact mutation.  
Use PlayTester / dedicated QA / local harnesses / non-mutating inspection. Clean up temporary QA mutations when practical.

Reports must state: Sora mutated YES/NO · Twinkle mutated YES/NO · QA account · mutations · cleanup (never claim cleanup if state was intentionally kept).

## Admin QA

Separate admin RPC + server auth check + distinct audit source.  
Do **not** weaken normal player cooldowns for admin convenience. Same grant machinery where practical. Normal users must not invoke admin QA.

## Build

Use `tools/stamp-build.js` / `build.json`. Do not casually edit build IDs in many HTML files by hand.  
Never `git reset --hard` / `git clean -fd` without inspecting state — do not discard owner work.

## Testing honesty

Do not report PASS from static inspection, synthetic HTML, mocked geometry, or a different DOM path alone.

Distinguish: STATIC PASS · LOCAL HARNESS PASS · REAL DOM PASS · REAL RPC PASS · PRODUCTION PASS.

Owner production observation overrides synthetic local PASS — investigate the real production DOM/path.

Screenshot-driven fixes: treat the image as symptom evidence; trace real DOM/CSS/render/asset/state.

## Owner-review closure

Report: BUILD before/after · commit · deploy state · root cause · implementation · QA (viewports + real DOM/RPC) · unchanged authority · player data · known limitations · verdict · next gate.  
If final release smoke is paused, say so explicitly and STOP.
